&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FINANCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab’s Finance team is responsible for all financial transactions for the company, operating as a well-oiled machine to maximize the value of our work. Our Finance team are made up of planners, analysts and accountants, and manage our policies, compliance, and reporting. They’re the ones who keep our financial operations in check, always thinking ahead and taking care to meet all of our financial, business, and government obligations. They’re attentive, diligent, and meticulous, and are mission-critical to Rocket Lab.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FINANCIAL ANALYST II&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based onsite at Rocket Lab&#39;s global headquarters in Long Beach, CA, the Financial Analyst will be responsible for the financial reporting of the enterprise, strategic projects, revenue and margin analysis, and other ad-hoc financial reporting. This position requires the ability to critically think, analyze large data sets and effectively communicate issues and opportunities in the business. A self-starter that excels in data analytics and problem solving will thrive in this role. The financial analyst will report to the FP&amp;amp;A manager and work closely with CFO, Corporate Controller, and a wide range of team members throughout the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL GET TO DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support budgeting and strategic planning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and assist in developing global processes that are scalable, streamlined and effective in meeting the evolving needs of a dynamic business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide timely and accurate financial information and recommendations to decision makers to make prudent business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect, analyze and manage data and create meaningful reports to drive business improvement and cost reductions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development and maintenance of weekly and monthly financial reporting, planning, and KPI’s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate current project spend and support ad-hoc reporting on spend rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support sales and marketing on customer proposals, pricing and opportunity forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting and analysis of monthly spend variances at cost center level liaising with cost center owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties or special projects as requested.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU&#39;LL BRING THESE QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience and a bachelor&#39;s degree in accounting, finance or similar, or equivalent years of work experience (6+ years working).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial analysis in a corporate environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THESE QUALIFICATIONS WOULD BE NICE TO HAVE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
