&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT ROCKET LAB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab is an end-to-end space company delivering responsive launch services, complete spacecraft design and manufacturing, payloads, satellite components, and more – all with the goal of opening access to space. The rockets and satellites we build and launch enable some of the most ambitious and vital space missions globally, supporting scientific exploration, Earth observation and missions to combat climate change, national security, and exciting new technology demonstrations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Electron rocket&amp;nbsp;has become the second most frequently launched U.S. rocket annually and has delivered more than 230 satellites to orbit, all while we work to develop Neutron, our upcoming medium-lift, reusable launch vehicle for larger constellation deployment. Our Space Systems business designs and builds our extensive line of satellites, payloads, and their components, including spacecraft that have been selected to support NASA missions to the Moon and Mars and components used on the James Webb Space Telescope.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1028198769?h=22add6027e&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab’s IT team&amp;nbsp;is responsible for&amp;nbsp;how our global teams access information and run operations across our computer systems, networks, and devices. Our hardworking IT team is a group of flexible problem-solvers working in a fast-paced&amp;nbsp;environment&amp;nbsp;but who also thrive under the challenge of supporting&amp;nbsp;all of&amp;nbsp;our proprietary systems and people, from finance to launch operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IT DATABASE ADMINISTRATOR II&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based onsite at Rocket Lab in Mt Wellington, Auckland, NZ the IT Database Administrator II will work closely with the US counterpart to deliver world class SQL Server services to Rocket Lab sites across the globe. You will be expected to collaborate with teams from ERP, BI, software development and other IT functions. The ideal candidate will have deep expertise in SQL Server environments and will be responsible for ensuring the availability, performance, security, and integrity of our mission-critical database systems.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT&amp;nbsp;YOU’LL&amp;nbsp;GET TO DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and&amp;nbsp;maintain&amp;nbsp;on-prem and cloud&amp;nbsp;SQL Server database environments (2016/2019/2022)&amp;nbsp;across Rocket Lab&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage database availability groups, replication, and failover&amp;nbsp;clustering&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform database installations, upgrades, patches, and&amp;nbsp;migrations&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor database&amp;nbsp;uptime,&amp;nbsp;performance&amp;nbsp;&amp;amp; resources, resolve performance issues, advise on&amp;nbsp;query&amp;nbsp;optimization&amp;nbsp;and table indexing&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure robust&amp;nbsp;backup and recovery strategies with tested disaster recovery procedures&amp;nbsp;are in place&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with regulatory requirements (GDPR, HIPAA, SOX, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide senior-level technical support for database-related issues&amp;nbsp;across all Rocket Lab sites&amp;nbsp;and ensure effective collaboration&amp;nbsp;/ handover&amp;nbsp;with the USA Senior DBA&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with application support and development teams to deliver robust and high performing business solutions&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and&amp;nbsp;maintain&amp;nbsp;comprehensive&amp;nbsp;global&amp;nbsp;documentation of database systems and procedures&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU’LL&amp;nbsp;BRING THESE&amp;nbsp;QUALIFICATIONS:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in IT and a bachelor&#39;s degree OR equivalent years of work experience (9+ years total experience)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of&amp;nbsp;experience in&amp;nbsp;database focused technology role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Microsoft Certified: Azure Database Administrator Associate or similar certification&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THESE QUALIFICATIONS&amp;nbsp;WOULD BE&amp;nbsp;NICE TO&amp;nbsp;HAVE:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of&amp;nbsp;experience in SQL Server Database Administration&amp;nbsp;in a&amp;nbsp;distributed&amp;nbsp;multi-instance server environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Azure SQL Database and managed instances&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of PowerShell scripting for automation&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Windows Server administration and storage systems&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with database monitoring tools (SolarWinds,&amp;nbsp;RedGate,&amp;nbsp;Idera, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with&amp;nbsp;migration and support of&amp;nbsp;cloud platforms (Azure, AWS)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of DevOps practices and CI/CD pipelines&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with other database platforms (Oracle, PostgreSQL, MySQL)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of data warehousing and ETL processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position may require prolonged periods of sitting, standing, walking, computer work, and occasional exposure to moderate levels of noise, dust, and fumes in production areas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
