&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT ROCKET LAB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab is an end-to-end space company delivering responsive launch services, complete spacecraft design and manufacturing, payloads, satellite components, and more – all with the goal of opening access to space. The rockets and satellites we build and launch enable some of the most ambitious and vital space missions globally, supporting scientific exploration, Earth observation and missions to combat climate change, national security, and exciting new technology demonstrations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Electron rocket&amp;nbsp;has become the second most frequently launched U.S. rocket annually and has delivered more than 230 satellites to orbit, all while we work to develop Neutron, our upcoming medium-lift, reusable launch vehicle for larger constellation deployment. Our Space Systems business designs and builds our extensive line of satellites, payloads, and their components, including spacecraft that have been selected to support NASA missions to the Moon and Mars and components used on the James Webb Space Telescope.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1028198769?h=22add6027e&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUPPLY CHAIN&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab’s Supply Chain team is responsible for the flow of all materials, products, and components through the business. With many of our own products functioning as critical components to our own and our customers’ missions, the Supply Chain team has a direct impact on the success of our rocket and satellite programs. They set up the assembly kits that enables our technicians to put together our Electron rockets, manage inventory, look after shipping and receiving, manage direct and indirect procurement, and inspect and ensure that all of our materials and products are compliant and up to standard. They are the chain that links our teams together, and are critical to our success.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEAD SUPPLIER QUALITY ENGINEER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based out of Rocket Lab&#39;s Long Beach, CA facility, the Lead Supplier Quality Engineer is responsible for ensuring that the quality requirements for procured parts and processes are consistently met. Leading a team of highly capable Supplier Quality Engineers, you will act as a key liaison between internal stakeholders and suppliers, translating complex technical requirements into clear, achievable specifications. Your exceptional leadership, communication, and negotiation skills will inspire suppliers to continuously improve, implement robust quality processes, and drive cost reduction and process efficiency, all while balancing the priorities of internal teams and external partners. This role also involves overseeing the creation of non-conformance reports, conducting supplier audits, managing supplier concessions, and identifying opportunities for improvement to reduce risk, cost, and lead time for Rocket Lab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET TO DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead high-performing teams by fostering collaboration, driving accountability, and empowering team members to achieve exceptional results in dynamic and challenging environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement robust supplier quality systems and processes to ensure consistent delivery of quality components and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize tools and metrics to monitor supplier performance, providing visibility into quality trends and driving accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives to improve purchased product quality, reduce non-conformances, and enhance supplier processes through root cause analysis and corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support suppliers in scaling production processes to meet future quality, cost, and delivery targets while introducing new products into production (NPI, APQP, PPAP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a bridge between suppliers, internal teams, and senior management to ensure alignment on technical requirements, production goals, and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS YOU’LL BRING AS A LEAD SUPPLIER QUALITY ENGINEER:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a quality role, preferably in regulated industries such as Aerospace, Medical, Automotive, or Industrial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical, Electrical, Aerospace, Mechatronic Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of quality systems, engineering drawings, GD&amp;amp;T, and specialized manufacturing processes like fabrication, CNC, PCBAs, and 3D printing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in root cause analysis tools (8D, 5 Whys, Fishbone diagrams, etc.) and practical problem-solving methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead projects, manage supplier relationships, and drive quality improvements across the supply chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Sit at desk and&amp;nbsp;operate&amp;nbsp;computer,&amp;nbsp;keyboard&amp;nbsp;and office equipment for extended periods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
