&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT ROCKET LAB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab is an end-to-end space company delivering responsive launch services, complete spacecraft design and manufacturing, payloads, satellite components, and more – all with the goal of opening access to space. The rockets and satellites we build and launch enable some of the most ambitious and vital space missions globally, supporting scientific exploration, Earth observation and missions to combat climate change, national security, and exciting new technology demonstrations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Electron rocket&amp;nbsp;has become the second most frequently launched U.S. rocket annually and has delivered more than 230 satellites to orbit, all while we work to develop Neutron, our upcoming medium-lift, reusable launch vehicle for larger constellation deployment. Our Space Systems business designs and builds our extensive line of satellites, payloads, and their components, including spacecraft that have been selected to support NASA missions to the Moon and Mars and components used on the James Webb Space Telescope.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1028198769?h=22add6027e&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ELECTRON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-end=&quot;326&quot;&gt;Rocket Lab’s Electron team builds, tests, and launches the Electron rocket across facilities in New Zealand and the United States. As one of the world’s most frequently launched rockets, Electron’s success is driven by a fast-moving, high-performing team committed to delivering reliable launch capability time and time again.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;328&quot; data-end=&quot;691&quot;&gt;At the core of this success is Rocket Lab’s Manufacturing team -&amp;nbsp; the builders and problem-solvers who bring rockets, satellites, and critical space systems to life. Working with advanced machinery and cutting-edge manufacturing technologies, including 3D printing, the team transforms engineering designs into high-quality hardware delivered on time and at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;693&quot; data-end=&quot;977&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;Rocket Lab is at the forefront of space innovation and is seeking talented Mechanical, Aerospace, and Manufacturing Engineers to join the team. If you meet at least 50% of the listed requirements, we encourage you to apply, as multiple opportunities are available across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MANUFACTURING ENGINEER II - MECHANICAL ASSEMBLY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will enable the production team to achieve required production rates while maintaining the highest quality standards. You’ll play a critical role in supporting all aspects of production at Rocket Lab by taking ownership of products released to production, removing production blockers, dispositioning non-conformance tickets, performing root-cause analysis, and implementing corrective actions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also be responsible for developing, implementing, and continuously improving manufacturing processes and procedures. Leveraging your strong working knowledge of both the product and best-practice manufacturing techniques, you’ll work closely with the production team to optimize processes, develop manufacturing best practices, and implement new processes through prototyping, testing, and integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU’LL BRING THESE QUALIFICATIONS:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and risk mitigation skills with proven experience in a manufacturing setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in Mechanical, Aerospace, or Manufacturing Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in technical documentation and project ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PLM/ERP systems and lean manufacturing principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in new product implementation and tooling design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THESE QUALIFICATIONS WOULD BE NICE TO HAVE: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in environmental/production testing (vibration, shock, thermal, vacuum).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of instrumentation (power supplies, accelerometers, thermocouples, RTDs, pressure sensors).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rocket Lab, you’ll have the opportunity to work on cutting-edge aerospace projects, tackle exciting challenges, and contribute to shaping the future of space exploration. If you’re ready to take your career to new heights, apply now and join us in redefining what’s possible in the aerospace industry!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us in shaping the future of space exploration!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
