&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1028198769?h=22add6027e&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ELECTRON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab’s Electron team is responsible for building, testing, and launching our Electron rocket across our launch sites and test facilities in the United States and New Zealand. Electron is one of the world’s most frequently-launched rockets, and our team behind its success are diligent, move fast, and have each others’ back to deliver a reliable rocket to the launch pad time and time again.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Rocket Lab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Rocket Lab is a global leader in launch and space systems. Our mission is to open access to space to improve life on Earth. We design, manufacture, and launch advanced rockets and spacecraft, enabling innovation for commercial, civil, defense, and academic customers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Manufacturing Engineer II – Vehicle Integration, you will enable Rocket Lab’s production teams to achieve required production rates with the highest quality. You will take ownership of products released to production, remove blockers, disposition non-conformance tickets, perform root-cause analysis, and implement corrective actions. You will also drive the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of manufacturing processes and procedures, leveraging your strong working knowledge of both the product and best-practice manufacturing techniques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Non-Conformance Support:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, analyze, and resolve manufacturing discrepancies and non-conformances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use substantiated engineering judgment and risk assessment to disposition non-conformances on flight hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead problem containment and root cause/corrective action investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with production teams to identify and drive quality-related initiatives and improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform structured root cause analysis of in-process failures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise between production, quality, supply chain, and design engineering for complex problem solving and process changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product, Process, and Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of assigned products that are production-ready, acting as subject matter expert&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain product manuals and lessons-learned documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute product improvements, including design and qualification activities&lt;/li&gt;
