&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT ROCKET LAB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rocket Lab is an end-to-end space company delivering responsive launch services, complete spacecraft design and manufacturing, payloads, satellite components, and more – all with the goal of opening access to space. The rockets and satellites we build and launch enable some of the most ambitious and vital space missions globally, supporting scientific exploration, Earth observation and missions to combat climate change, national security, and exciting new technology demonstrations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Electron rocket&amp;nbsp;has become the second most frequently launched U.S. rocket annually and has delivered more than 230 satellites to orbit, all while we work to develop Neutron, our upcoming medium-lift, reusable launch vehicle for larger constellation deployment. Our Space Systems business designs and builds our extensive line of satellites, payloads, and their components, including spacecraft that have been selected to support NASA missions to the Moon and Mars and components used on the James Webb Space Telescope.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1028198769?h=22add6027e&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SPACE SYSTEMS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rocket Lab, we’re not just launching rockets — we&#39;re building the future of space. Our Space Systems team builds everything from complete spacecraft, precision payloads to the components and subsystems that allow them to thrive in space, like solar panels, flight software, star trackers, optical systems, separation systems, radios, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Space Systems team has enabled more than 1,700 missions, ranging from interplanetary exploration, in-space manufacturing to national security and defense initiatives. The team has built spacecraft, payloads, and components for missions to the Moon and Mars, working with partners including NASA, the Space Development Agency, and the U.S. Space Force. Whether it’s a single high-performance spacecraft, constellation, or the vertically integrated components that help them get to space — our world class Space Systems team is empowering some of the boldest and most ambitious space missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SENIOR MASTER SCHEDULER II&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based onsite at Rocket Lab&#39;s global headquarters in Long Beach, CA, the Senior Master Scheduler II is a centerpiece of all schedule-related activities supporting Space Systems development and manufacturing. In this role, you aren’t just managing a schedule; you are optimizing a high-velocity value chain. You will be counted on to identify missing pieces in day-to-day operations, support the implementation of process improvements, and help drive new scheduling norms across the Space Systems group. Our ideal candidate is an assertive, creative thinker who loves building best practices and improving processes in a fast-paced, technically focused environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET TO DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and analyze schedules for Rocket Lab Space Systems programs. Ensure vertical and horizontal integration across all program tiers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure schedules are aligned with project objectives and resource availability. Identify potential bottlenecks and support the development of mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Project Managers, Engineering, and Supply Chain to gather accurate data and ensure program signals are reflected with surgical precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and deliver timely schedule reports and dashboards. You will help apprise Program Managers of schedule performance and &quot;margin erosion.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain scheduling tools and processes (using ERP/MRP, SQL, or PowerBI) that improve the efficiency and quality of reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear priorities to production teams and manage &quot;push/pull&quot; signals to reduce lead times and ensure delivery targets are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support root cause analysis for schedule slips and help implement scalable solutions using Lean, Six Sigma, or Kaizen principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS YOU’LL BRING:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience as a Scheduler in a New Space, Aerospace, or other technical industry, and a bachelor’s degree or equivalent years of work experience (12+ years of total work experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detailed knowledge and familiarity with MS Project and JIRA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to read technical documentation and understand complex hardware assembly sequences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP/MRP systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic experience writing SQL queries or building data visualizations (IE. Power BI) to track health metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;U.S citizenship is required, due to program requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THESE QUALIFICATIONS WOULD BE NICE TO HAVE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and take ownership of projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infor LN ERP experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to VBA or Python to automate scheduling workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. Top Secret Security Clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
